Z||000016||Jncomutt||12-10-2001||10:59 PM||||In 85, the gauges on the v6 only read up to 85.  They didn't get the 120 speedometer til 86.  I just want to know what the rear bumper looks like.  I noticed its a V6, but doesn't have aero lower body.  Duel exhaust, if it has it, probably looks out of place on the coupe bumper.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Galen||12-11-2001||12:23 AM||||why would it look out of place? 85 se v6's were coupes.. with the black bumpers..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/galen-sig-xmas3.gif">  <BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT></B> - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||BlackStang95||12-11-2001||03:32 AM||||V6 fieros were produced in far less numbers than the 4 cylinder models.  This makes the number still in existence today fairly low.  I'd say a v6 fiero is uncommon but not rare yet.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Blacktree||12-11-2001||04:37 AM||||Ugh, those wheels look like they came from a pickup truck.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Hartz||12-11-2001||08:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>In 85, the gauges on the v6 only read up to 85.  They didn't get the 120 speedometer til 86.  I just want to know what the rear bumper looks like.  I noticed its a V6, but doesn't have aero lower body.  Duel exhaust, if it has it, probably looks out of place on the coupe bumper.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>In 1985 you could get the V6 without the aero body.  Just a plain ol' bumper coupe SE with a V6.  And yes, they had dual exhaust, and no, they didn't look that bad.<P>I know the speedometers only went to 85 MPH, but look at the font on the guages.  They don't match.  Here, look at these pictures:<P>This is an 85 MPH guage cluster out of a 4 cylinder car:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84_guage_1.JPG"> <P>This is an 85 MPH guage cluster out of a V6 car:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_gt_guage_1.jpg"> <P>I know they're not the best pictures in the world, but notice the differences in the font on the guages themselves.  Now go back and look at the car for sale - the tach is one style and the speedo is another.  Since the odometer is attached to the speedo, and the speedo doesn't match...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>Hartz||||reg||1
Z||000021||ChopTop||12-11-2001||11:59 AM||||Good eye Hartz.  I have a "rare" 85SE V6, dual exhaust, and 85 speedo.  Now I have to go look and see what my dash looks like!||||reg||1
Z||000022||ProudGT||12-11-2001||12:44 PM||||Notice that the speedometer is setting at about 10 MPH in all of the pictures, even the one with the driver's door wide open. Couldn't help but notice that the tach is setting at 2300 RPM in all of the pictures. It doesn't appear to burn any oil cranked up at that rate, but the oil pressure looks low on the gauge.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Hartz||12-11-2001||01:34 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChopTop:<BR><B>...I have a "rare" 85SE V6, dual exhaust, and 85 speedo...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Me too!  I suspect that your guage cluster will look just like the second picture, only your idiot lights will not be outlined in orange, but rather have the style of the cluster above it.  In the photos, those are swapped from stock.  <P>I had never even seen a four cylinder guage cluster until I got my '84 - that was why it was so noticeable to me.<P>I'm not saying the guy is lying or anything, it just looks very suspicious.<P>Hartz<p>[This message has been edited by Hartz (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
